<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">scout</ansi>

See how the enemy groups here stand before you fight them. Scouting is free:
it takes no skill and no time, and works in a fight, on a group waiting its
turn, or on one that hasn't noticed you.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">scout</ansi>
  List the enemy groups here, with their numbers and what they're doing.

  <ansi fg="command">scout [group]</ansi>
  Draw a group's formation, front row nearest you, with each member's
  health: <ansi fg="command">scout ruffians</ansi>.

  A band of ruffians, as they stand (front row nearest you):
          col 1                   col 2                   col 3
  front [ *ruffian (unhurt)     |  ruffian (wounded)    | ------ ]
  mid   [  cutpurse (unhurt)    | ------                | ------ ]
  back  [ ------                |  rat (unhurt)         | ------ ]
  * you can reach them from your place in the formation.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Reading it</ansi>

- A <ansi fg="yellow">*</ansi> marks the members you can reach from your place in your company's
  formation (what <ansi fg="command">formation reach</ansi> tells you). Move in the formation
  before you <ansi fg="command">attack</ansi> if you can't reach the ones you want.
- The front of each column takes the first blows: plain melee reaches only
  the front, a reach weapon one rank deeper, and a bow anyone.
- Health reads unhurt, scratched, wounded, badly wounded, or near death.
- Below the grid, a Burdened line names the members whose own load
  burdens them (lightly burdened, burdened, or heavily burdened): they
  dodge less (<ansi fg="command">help burden</ansi>). The unburdened aren't listed.
- The formation changes as members fall: the one behind steps up.

In the web client, the Combat tab's Battle view shows your battle's group
the same way, with the same words, and keeps it current (<ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>).

You see what <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> sees: hidden members are left out, and in the dark
you can't make them out. <ansi fg="command">look [group]</ansi> describes a group in words.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help attack</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help targeting</ansi>.
